**Wave 35 moved seven of those rungs and the two ladders still agree at the bottom on
RATIO.** Sealed 1/15 and canonical 1/15 and 2/15 all land on `ARCH.V12CL896X13` at
0.420779x — 42.1 per cent of the parent, and *below* the `ARCH.V8CL896` content death at
0.432784x. Sealed 2/15 moves to `ARCH.V9CL896` at 0.437349x, which halves the campaign's
0/15 bracket to 0.004565 of stored ratio — 1,024 vocabulary rows between a child that
answers nothing and a child that summarises an update and lists four missing quantities.
Sealed 3/15 moves to `ARCH.V10CL896G03` at 0.441915x. The sealed 4/15 rung does not move:
`ARCH.V12CL896G03` at 0.451045x keeps it.

At the three rung the two ladders now name DIFFERENT CHILDREN at the same ratio, because
`ARCH.V10CL896G01` reaches three canonically on a lane the frozen protocol seals a miss.
That is the first time the ladders have diverged on identity while agreeing on depth.

The eight rung is the only interior rung the two readings agree on:
`ARCH.V16CL1792` at 0.637073x reads eight either way.

**Twenty of the twenty-four children ever built below half the parent hold at least one
case on at least one standard**, and `DEEP_RECORD.md` lists all twenty-four.
`ARCH.V19CL896G03` and `ARCH.V20CL896G03` hold **four of fifteen at 0.483x and 0.488x** —
the supplier summary, the vendor email, the missing-quantities request, and 4:15 p.m.
pulled off the note. `ARCH.V19X13CL896` and `ARCH.KKTS`, both sealed at **zero**, are not
zero: one compresses the supplier update and lands the one-week expansion risk, the other
orders a migration backups-then-TLS-then-verify and names the four withheld quantities.

Three children in the whole campaign are honest content deaths — readable, fluent,
on-register and empty: `ARCH.KKTD` (0.483x), `ARCH.V8CL896` (0.433x) and `ARCH.X12`
(0.952x). The last of those is the control that matters: content death is not a function
of depth.

## THE SEALED COLUMNS, unchanged

Everything below this line is the wave-33 file as sealed. No number in it was
edited. It is the frozen-fifteen reading, and it remains the only column any
ledger row, verdict or seal fires on.

**READ THE REVIEW COLUMN AS AN UPPER BOUND, and wave 33 is the first wave that
can say by how much.** The sealed fifteen is a reading of one wording of each
ask. `wave33/robustness-frontier.json` re-asks every sealed-held lane in three
restatements and counts the ones that still answer:

| child | net | sealed 15 | **robust** |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| PARENT | 1.000000 | 12 | **6** |
| `ARCH.B75` | 0.742049 | 11 | **2** |
| `ARCH.V19X13G03` | 0.742049 | 11 | **2** |
| `ARCH.V18X13` | 0.737484 | 10 | **3** |
| `ARCH.V16CL1792` | 0.637073 | 8 | **2** |
| `ARCH.CL1792M` | 0.856199 | 8 | **0** |
| `ARCH.V12CL1792` | 0.618813 | 7 | **1** |
| `ARCH.V8CL1792` | 0.600552 | 5 | **2** |

**The sealed ordering does not survive rewording.** `ARCH.V18X13` is more robust
than `ARCH.B75` and deeper; `ARCH.V8CL1792` at sealed five is as robust as
`ARCH.B75` at sealed eleven; and `ARCH.CL1792M` — the reader-metric body that
reads one case BETTER than its stream-selected twin — holds **none** of its eight
under a restatement. The parent holds six of its ten scorable lanes, so this is
not an impossible bar. Two of the fifteen lanes are unscorable for everyone
because the paraphrase bank dropped the note and the update its own prompts refer
to; that defect is charged to the bank and stated in the artifact.

The restatement column is a **diagnostic** under the canonical standard, not a gate:
it measures how narrowly a retained behaviour is addressed, which is a different
question from whether the behaviour is retained at all.

**The `ARCH.V16CL1792` ≥8 rung at 0.637073x stays retired**, and wave 33 added a
second cell to it: `ARCH.GV16L01` ties that 8/15 exactly, holding the same eight
lanes including the same `creative-continuity` case that fails all three
restatements. **The campaign's honest deep frontier remains `ARCH.V12CL1792` at
7/15, 0.618813x** under the sealed reading, and wave 33 moved no frontier row at
any of the fifteen thresholds: the deepest stored ratio at every one of them is
the number wave 32's table already carried. Under the canonical standard that
seven-of-fifteen row is `ARCH.V8CL1792` at 0.600552x instead.

**The second review surface, bounded.** ADDENDUM 16.1's 30-prompt extension bank
prices and orders; it grades nothing, and wave 33 measured what it can price.
Pooled over **sixty child observations across four waves** on one frozen bank its
Spearman is **0.6926**, and it is reproducible to the byte: two children decoded
in wave 31 and again in wave 32 score identically and hold the identical prompt
set. Its resolution, by sealed gap: **48.1% agreement and 34.5% inversions at one
case, 81.6% at four, 100% at ten and beyond.** So it may be used to order two
children four or more cases apart and may **not** be used to price a one-case
margin, which is the job it was built for. The per-wave verdict string is retired:
a null holding the instrument fixed and varying only the population puts wave 32's
`SCRAMBLED` 0.3537 at the 8th percentile and wave 31's `VALIDATED` 0.7411 at the
89th, on a 90% interval of 0.31–0.79 — wider than the gap between the scorer's own
thresholds. Every count in this file is the frozen fifteen, read by hand, exactly
as it has been for thirty-three waves.

